{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/PerformingCalibration"],"anchor":"Articles","title":"Articles"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"getTestContexts()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns a stream of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" updates for the traces in the currently configured test. The first values you receive give you a complete set of contexts for the configured traces, and later values let you observe how those contexts change over time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" identifies a trace by ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and carries that trace’s current ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TraceContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Trace contexts also include the current calibration status for the trace. Depending on the trace type, they may also include related information such as the last calibration time or when calibration is next due.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Why-test-contexts-are-streamed","type":"heading","text":"Why test contexts are streamed"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Trace readiness can change while your app is running. A trace might become runnable after an instrument connects, or it might stop being runnable if the device reports a new problem.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That is why test contexts are exposed as a stream instead of a one-shot result: they represent current runtime state, not just configuration-time state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Understand-blockers","type":"heading","text":"Understand blockers"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The most important part of a trace context is its blocker list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each concrete trace-context type has its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blockers"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A trace will only actually run when that list is empty."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the blocker list is not empty, the trace is not runnable yet. That does not always mean the test is permanently invalid. It often means your app needs to wait for, fix, or communicate some current condition first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some examples include:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instrumentNotConnected"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"batteryLow","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rtfNotZeroed","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, the blocker list is the quickest way to answer the question, “Can this trace run right now?”","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Use-the-stream-in-your-app","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Use the stream in your app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Applications typically consume "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getTestContexts()"},{"type":"text","text":" to keep UI or workflow state aligned with trace readiness."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, you might show blockers in the UI, disable a “Run Test” action while any trace still has blockers, or prompt the user to connect an instrument before trying again.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["for try await context in unify.getTestContexts() {","    print(\"Trace \\(context.traceIndex) updated: \\(context.traceContext)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The exact blocker list depends on the concrete trace type, so apps usually inspect the specific trace context they care about and then read its "},{"code":"blockers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property."}]},{"anchor":"Relationship-to-test-configuration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Relationship to test configuration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you call "},{"code":"configureTest(test:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the returned "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestConfigurationResult"},{"type":"text","text":" includes initial trace contexts for the configured test."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use those initial contexts as the starting snapshot, then use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getTestContexts()"},{"type":"text","text":" to observe ongoing updates after configuration."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How to decide whether a trace is ready to run."}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/testcontexts"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Understanding Test Contexts","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Unify3Sdk"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestContexts"},"references":{"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sd